{"name":"Blue-Collar","hex":"#005f7a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue-collar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Working class; engaged or trained in essentially manual labor.","Pertaining to the culture of blue-collar workers."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blue-collar worker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue-collar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue-collar worker","blocks":[{"text":"A blue-collar worker is a person who performs manual labor or skilled trades. Originating and used most frequently in the United States, the term 'Blue-collar work' may involve skilled or unskilled labor. The type of work may involve manufacturing, warehousing, mining, carpentry, electrical work, custodial work, agriculture, logging, landscaping, food processing, waste collection and disposal, construction, shipping, and many other types of physical work that typically do not require higher education. Blue-collar work often involves something being physically built or maintained. In social status, blue-collar workers generally belong to the working class."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Mechanic_at_work.jpg/330px-Mechanic_at_work.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-collar_worker","wikidata":"Q1191714"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg/500px-AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg/1280px-AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg/500px-AlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A welder making boilers at the Combustion Engineering Company in Chattanooga, Tennessee in June 1942. Despite their name, blue-collar workers do not always or typically wear blue shirts.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlfredPalmerwelder1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/PV-Anlage_Zugspitze_Montage.jpg/500px-PV-Anlage_Zugspitze_Montage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/PV-Anlage_Zugspitze_Montage.jpg/500px-PV-Anlage_Zugspitze_Montage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Workers constructing a photovoltaic system on the Zugspitze, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APV-Anlage_Zugspitze_Montage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Photo_by_Mona_Mijthab%2C_July_2011_%286349812257%29.jpg/500px-Photo_by_Mona_Mijthab%2C_July_2011_%286349812257%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Photo_by_Mona_Mijthab%2C_July_2011_%286349812257%29.jpg/500px-Photo_by_Mona_Mijthab%2C_July_2011_%286349812257%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A textile factory outside Dhaka, Bangladesh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_by_Mona_Mijthab%2C_July_2011_(6349812257).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Municipal_recycling_facilities%2C_Montgomery_County%2C_MD._2007%2C_Credit_USEPA_%2814410405277%29.jpg/500px-Municipal_recycling_facilities%2C_Montgomery_County%2C_MD._2007%2C_Credit_USEPA_%2814410405277%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Municipal_recycling_facilities%2C_Montgomery_County%2C_MD._2007%2C_Credit_USEPA_%2814410405277%29.jpg/500px-Munici